DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     A lliibbxxoo handle can be allocated using the xxoo__ccrreeaattee() function.

             Example:
               xo_handle_t *xop = xo_create(XO_STYLE_JSON, XOF_WARN);
               ....
               xo_emit_h(xop, "testing\n");

     By default, lliibbxxoo writes output to standard output.  A convenience func‐
     tion is provided for situations when output should be written to a dif‐
     ferent file.

     Use the XOF_CLOSE_FP flag to trigger a call to fclose(3) for the FILE
     pointer when the handle is destroyed.

     The xxoo__ddeessttrrooyy() function releases a handle and any resources it is us‐
     ing.  Calling xxoo__ddeessttrrooyy() with a NULL handle will release any resources
     associated with the default handle.

